Advance through the input when Schannel splits a write into records.
tls_write encrypts at most one maximum-size record (16 KiB) at a time,
but never moved buf past the part it had sent, so every record after the
first repeated the first 16 KiB. Any single read over 16 KiB that the
TLS copy loop passed on was corrupted, e.g. a large "wget --post-file"
over https sent the wrong body. Step buf along with len.

---
 networking/tls.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/networking/tls.c
+++ b/networking/tls.c
@@ -3451,6 +3451,7 @@
 			   buffers[0].cbBuffer + buffers[1].cbBuffer +
 			   buffers[2].cbBuffer);
 
+		buf += copy_amount;
 		len -= copy_amount;
 	}
 }
